# Deployment Conventions

## Provisioning New Agents

Always use `create-instance.sh` -- never hand-build triplets:
```bash
./multi-instance-deploy/create-instance.sh <instance-number>
```

Instance number determines:
- IP addresses: 172.23.88.N (agent), 172.23.89.N (homeserver)
- Port mappings: derived from instance number
- Container names: agent<N>, continuwuity<N>, caddy<N>

## Templates

Templates in `multi-instance-deploy/templates/` are the source of truth:
- `docker-compose.yml.template` -- Agent triplet compose
- `Caddyfile.template` -- Per-agent TLS config
- `matrix-mcp-server/` -- Has its own package.json and CLAUDE.md
- `matrix-bot/` -- Rust (primary) and Python (legacy)
- `scripts/` -- Fleet management, sync, switch, smoke-test

## Host Scripts

`multi-instance-deploy/scripts/` contains host-side helpers:
- `destroy-and-rebuild.sh` -- Full agent teardown and rebuild
- `fix-agentX-services.sh` -- Service repair scripts

Never modify templates without considering impact on existing deployed agents.
